{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Personal Minicomputers, PC", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about minicomputers. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify information about the history of software and its characteristics in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "There Be in Simple Past Negative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>there was</strong> or <strong>there were</strong> to talk about the existence of something in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we want to say that something did not exist or that didn't take place in the past, we can use <strong>there was</strong> or <strong>there were</strong> in its <strong>negative form</strong>: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<center><strong>There</strong> + verb 'to be' in simple past and negative form (<strong>was not /were not</strong>) + complement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:</br> <strong><i>There were not</strong> many microcomputers at that time. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that we use <strong>there was</strong> when we talk about singular objects. On the other hand, we use <strong>there were</strong> when we talk about plural objects. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Let's take a look at the following examples:</br> <i><strong>There were not</strong> many microprocessors in 1960.</br> <strong>There was not</strong> any microprocessor in 1960.</i> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We can also use the contracted form of the <strong>verb 'to be'</strong> and the particle <strong>not</strong>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There were not = <strong>there weren't</strong></br>There was not = <strong>there wasn't</strong>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There wasn't any software at that time for programming computers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So, there weren't any competitors at that time for Microsoft, right?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There weren't many competitors for Apple.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Both to Refer to Two Nouns in a Pair", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>both</strong> to talk about two things that go together.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we want to show the relationship between two things, we can use <strong>both.</strong></br></br> Let's consider the following example:<br></br>  <i><strong>Both</strong> <b>Microsoft</b> and <b>Apple</b> made important innovations in the software industry. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We place <strong>both</strong> before the nouns that we are referring to. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><strong><i>Both</strong> the <b>price</b> and <b>size</b> of computers</u> were reduced for making computers more affordable. </br><b>Both Carlie </b>and <b>Joshua</b> understand the importance of microprocessors in computers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Both Paul Allen and Bill Gates liked to play with computers in high school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This was when both Steve Wozniak and Steve Jobs decided to build a computer called Apple I that was powered by the 6502 microprocessor.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "plug-in cards", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cards with new information that can be plugged in to the computer ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This means that you could add extra attributes by developing plug-in cards", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "success", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to achieve or fulfill a positive result of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After this success, microcomputers began to evolve even faster and they became cheaper.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "competitor", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a person or group of people that compete against another one", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So, there weren't any competitors at that time for Microsoft, right?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "microprocessor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a device in a computer that controls what the computer does", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There were not many people interested in buying the 4004 microprocessor at the beginning because people didn't know what to use microcomputers for.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "realize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gradually notice or to understand something gradually ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With the 8080 microprocessor, people realized that these devices were good enough for running small co