> Luisa</span>: Mark, what are you reading? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Mark</span>: I'm reading about the birth of microcomputers. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Luisa</span>: That sounds interesting. So, what does it say?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Mark</span>: Well, it starts by explaining that there were not many people interested in buying the 4004 microprocessor at the beginning because people didn't know what to use microcomputers for. However, in 1974, with the 8080 microprocessors, people realized that these devices were good enough for running small computers. After this success, microcomputers began to evolve even faster and they became cheaper. For example, the Altair microprocessor was a big success and one of its strengths was its open architecture. This means that you could add extra attributes by developing plug-in cards. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Luisa</span>: There wasn't any software at that time for programming computers, right?", "image": "enpe7n1le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "62000", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\"> Mark</span>: No. That's why Microsoft was invented. Both Paul Allen and Bill Gates liked to play with computers in high school and they decided to write Altair BASIC, an interpreter for computers. As the software they created was successful, they decided to found the Microsoft company. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Luisa</span>: So, there weren't any competitors at that time for Microsoft, right?", "image": "enpe7n1le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "87500", "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\"> Mark</span>: That's right, but not for long. As Altair was getting more popular, more people became interested in the subject. This was when both Steve Wozniak and Steve Jobs decided to build a computer called Apple I, that was powered by the 6502 microprocessor. This first computer was very popular and they soon started their business. By 1977, they released the Apple II which was a big success because it was very easy to use. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Luisa</span>: So, there weren't many competitors for Apple at that time. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Mark</span>: They were one of the most important companies. But the low cost and the ease of programming microcomputers brought a lot of new people into the software industry.", "image": "enpe7n1le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n1le02ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}